{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793350455,"nonce":"QpU2sXxuUPkDTYEDnas6Uac1Ers=","title":"Retain browser editor bindings during confirmed workspace moves","message":"Parent: 9d6a14bfc40bc5c2eb5a105609e1c2a1c37f3766d131dae8f4da586edd8b7b3c\n\nCoordinate initiating browser file/directory moves through existing native closed-document move support: drain prior editor requests and pending saves/updates, keep Yjs replicas and per-author undo managers alive, release transport subscriptions, perform an identity-preserving move, retarget bindings and tabs, then reopen by expected ID. Queue new edits while moving. Failed, refused moves resume the original bindings; uncertain or partially confirmed outcomes preserve recovery and pause affected documents. Other active clients remain protected by the native document-open guard.\n\nIntegrate Explorer rename, cut/paste and drag/drop with mutable Haxe binding paths and existing tab/history remapping. Preserve dirty recovery baselines, caret/selection, split editors and undo state. Keep hosted support disabled. Validate single-file and directory moves, pending updates/saves, queued typing, failed destination collisions, another active client, close/reconnect races and old-path recreation. Live cross-client move coordination, stable-ID personal-history persistence and hosted/cross-host integration remain on the parent.","files":null}]}